\subsection{Semantic search: alone, unfiltered, at most fifty}
\label{sec:search-semantic-checks}

[[-p openalex-semantic]] runs OpenAlex's search by meaning
(\cref{sec:openalex-semantic} in the providers chapter).  Its answer
is a ranked list of at most fifty works, not a count of matches, and
three things a keyword search allows would make that answer misleading
in the record, so the command refuses them before any request is made:
\begin{description}
\item[Other providers in the same search] Their results would be merged
  with the ranked list into one record whose count is neither a count
  nor a ranking.  A semantic check is its own search, recorded as such.
\item[Filters] The provider takes none (the providers chapter explains
  why); refusing here says so at once instead of recording a failed
  search.  This refusal looks at the [[SearchFilters]] the command
  builds, not at the filter options one by one, so a filter added
  later is refused without anyone remembering this place; it therefore
  sits right after the filters are built, in a chunk of its own.
\item[A question over 2\,000 characters] OpenAlex matches only the first
  2\,000 characters, so the recorded question would not be the one
  matched.
\end{description}
Each is a usage error, exit code 2 with one line saying what to change,
as for any other malformed command line.

The limit is different: a limit above fifty is not wrong, only more
than exists, and [[-l 0]] (\enquote{all}) means all fifty.  So the
limit is lowered to the provider's maximum rather than refused.  It is
lowered here, before the search, because the session records the limit
that was asked for, and [[prov found-via]] reproduces the search from
that record: the record should say [[--limit 50]], what was actually
asked for, not the [[1000]] of the default.

<<refuse what a semantic search cannot do>>=
ranked_names = [n for n in provider_names if is_ranked_provider(n)]
if ranked_names:
    from scholar.providers import OPENALEX_SEMANTIC_MAX_CHARS, get_provider

    ranked_name = ranked_names[0]
    if len(provider_names) > 1:
        refusal = (
            f"{ranked_name} must be the only provider of a search: it "
            f"returns a ranked list, not a count of matches."
        )
    elif len(query) > OPENALEX_SEMANTIC_MAX_CHARS:
        refusal = (
            f"{ranked_name} matches at most {OPENALEX_SEMANTIC_MAX_CHARS} "
            f"characters; this question has {len(query)}."
        )
    else:
        refusal = None
    if refusal:
        Console(stderr=True).print(f"[red]{escape(refusal)}[/red]")
        raise typer.Exit(2)
    ranked_max = getattr(get_provider(ranked_name), "MAX_LIMIT", None)
    if ranked_max and (limit == 0 or limit > ranked_max):
        limit = ranked_max
<<refuse filters for a semantic search>>=
if ranked_names and filters is not None and not filters.is_empty():
    Console(stderr=True).print(
        f"[red]{escape(ranked_names[0])} takes no filters.[/red]"
    )
    raise typer.Exit(2)
