\section{Research Questions}
\label{sec:research-questions}

The [[rq]] command starts from a research question rather than a fixed search
string.
It uses an LLM to translate the question into provider-specific search queries,
executes those searches, and then labels a subset of the results with
keep/discard decisions and themes/motivations.

The command is designed for iterative work:
\begin{description}
\item[Search] Generate one query per provider and fetch results.
\item[Label] Classify the first [[--count]] papers with the LLM.
\item[Review] The saved session can be opened later with [[scholar sessions resume]].
\end{description}

We include the same filter options as [[search]], so users can constrain results
by year, venue, open access, citation counts, and publication type.

