[[rq]] does not run the semantic search ([[openalex-semantic]],
\cref{sec:openalex-semantic}).  Everything [[rq]] does around a
provider assumes a keyword search: the model writes one keyword query
per provider, with boolean operators where the provider's rule allows
them, and none of the rules describes a question in plain words; the
providers' results go into one session next to each other; the limit
recorded is the keyword default; and the filters are applied to every
provider, which the semantic search refuses.  Run through [[rq]], it
would record a keyword-style query as a semantic search, mixed with
counts from the other providers.  So [[rq]] refuses it before the
research question is even asked for, and names the two commands that
run it properly: [[search -p openalex-semantic]] for a recorded check,
[[sessions check]] for one held against the sessions.

