\section{Enriching Papers}

The [[enrich]] command fetches missing abstracts/metadata for papers in a
review session.  This is useful when you've already done a search and want to
fill in abstracts without re-running the search.  It is also where a session
learns which of its papers are open access: the enrichment step consults
Unpaywall (\cref{unpaywall-module}) for every paper with a DOI, and the
command reports the tally.

A session can be large---thousands of papers---while the papers that
need attention now are few: those still pending after a new search,
which are about to be classified and need their abstracts first
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/137}).
Three options and one property of the command serve that case:
\begin{description}
\item[ [[--pending-only]] ] restricts the whole run to the papers still
  pending a decision.
\item[ [[--fields]] ] names what to fill, so a run that only wants
  abstracts can skip the open-access and preprint steps.
\item[ [[--enrich-providers]] ] reorders the providers; with OpenAlex
  first the run profits most from its batched DOI lookups
  (\cref{sec:openalex-doi-batch}).
\item[Saving as it goes] the session is saved after every chunk of
  papers, so a run cut short keeps what it has fetched
  (\cref{sec:enrich-chunks}).
\end{description}

<<enrich command>>=
@app.command()
def enrich(
    session: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Name of the review session to enrich.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    enrich_providers: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--enrich-providers",
            help=(
                "Comma-separated provider names to use for enrichment. "
                "Overrides the default order (s2, arxiv, openalex, ieee, "
                "wos, crossref, europepmc, scopus). Putting openalex first "
                "makes the most of its batched DOI lookups. An unknown "
                "name or an empty value is a usage error."
            ),
        ),
    ] = None,
    preprint_search: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--preprint-search",
            help=(
                "When no PDF is found, also search preprint servers by "
                "title and authors for a preprint version to adopt. "
                "Authoritative preprint links (OpenAlex, Crossref) are "
                "followed even without this flag."
            ),
        ),
    ] = False,
    pending_only: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--pending-only",
            help=(
                "Enrich and check only the papers still pending a "
                "decision; decided papers are left as they are."
            ),
        ),
    ] = False,
    fields: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--fields",
            help=(
                "Comma-separated fields to fill (default: "
                "abstract,pdf_url,keywords). pdf_url also turns on the "
                "Unpaywall open-access lookup and the preprint fallback. "
                "Valid: title, authors, abstract, year, venue, pdf_url, "
                "keywords."
            ),
        ),
    ] = None,
) -> None:
    """
    Fetch missing abstracts/metadata for papers in a review session.

    Looks up papers by DOI in available providers to fill in missing
    abstracts/metadata. Providers requiring API keys (IEEE, WoS) are used
    only when configured. Abstracts the other providers lack are asked of
    Crossref and Europe PMC before Scopus. Also looks up open-access
    status and PDF links
