\subsection{Choosing the fields}

The fields are those [[enrich_paper]] can fill
([[ENRICHMENT_FIELD_NAMES]], \cref{enrich-module}); the default is the
set the command always used.
A misspelt name would otherwise be passed on and never filled, and the
run would look like one that found nothing, so we reject it as a usage
error (exit status 2, like a bad [[--proxy]]) naming the valid choices.
The help text lists them too; it cannot read them from the enrichment
module, which the command imports only when it runs.
[[pdf_url]] is more than a field: [[enrich_paper]] runs the Unpaywall
lookup and the preprint fallback only when it is requested, so
[[--fields abstract]] is the cheap run that skips both.
The Crossref currency check is not a field and runs either way.

<<constants>>=
ENRICH_DEFAULT_FIELDS = ["abstract", "pdf_url", "keywords"]
<<enrich command>>=
def parse_enrich_fields(value: str | None) -> list[str]:
    """Return the field names in a `--fields` value, validated.

    Raises `typer.BadParameter` (exit status 2) for an unknown name.
    """
    from scholar.enrich import ENRICHMENT_FIELD_NAMES

    if value is None:
        return list(ENRICH_DEFAULT_FIELDS)
    names = [name.strip() for name in value.split(",") if name.strip()]
    unknown = [name for name in names if name not in ENRICHMENT_FIELD_NAMES]
    if unknown or not names:
        raise typer.BadParameter(
            f"unknown field(s): {', '.join(unknown) or '(none given)'}; "
            f"choose from {', '.join(ENRICHMENT_FIELD_NAMES)}",
            param_hint="'--fields'",
        )
    return names
@

\subsection{Choosing the sources}
\label{sec:enrich-provider-names}

[[--enrich-providers]] names the sources to ask and their order, for
[[scholar enrich]] and for [[scholar search --enrich]] alike.
A name nothing answers to used to be passed on and skipped without a
word, so a typo gave a run that asked fewer sources than the user
thought.
It is now a usage error, like an unknown field, naming the valid
choices: the registered providers with a DOI lookup and the abstract
services Crossref and Europe PMC ([[enrichment_source_names]],
\cref{sec:enrichment-providers}).
Without the option the enrichment's own default order applies, which
[[None]] stands for.
An empty value is an error too, not the default order: it names no
source, and a script that builds the list and ends up with none should
hear so.
[[scholar search]] checks the value as soon as the providers are known,
also without [[--enrich]], where it would otherwise be ignored: a typo
is then reported before the search spends any requests, and the next
run with [[--enrich]] does not meet it.
Both help texts say so.

<<enrich command>>=
def parse_enrich_providers(value: str | None) -> list[str] | None:
    """Return the source names in an `--enrich-providers` value.

    None (the default order) when not given. Raises
    `typer.BadParameter` (exit status 2) for a name no source has.
    """
    if value is None:
        return None
    from scholar.enrich import enrichment_source_names

    valid = enrichment_source_names()
    names = [name.strip() for name in value.split(",") if name.strip()]
    unknown = [name for name in names if name not in valid]
    if unknown or not names:
        raise typer.BadParameter(
            f"unknown source(s): {', '.join(unknown) or '(none given)'}; "
            f"choose from {', '.join(valid)}",
            param_hint="'--enrich-providers'",
        )
    return names
@

