The \enquote{Configured} cell marks the OpenAlex-backed preprint
providers with an asterisk ([[Yes*]]): they are configured (green) yet
deliberately absent from default searches, and without a marker those
two facts read as a contradiction.
The marker rides on the status word rather than the provider name
because every character added to the provider column---whose widest
entry is already [[researchsquare]]---is taken from the fold-prone
\enquote{How to Get Key} column at the standard 80-column width, and
because the name cells are copy-material that must stay pristine.
The footer explains the marker once instead of per row.

<<add provider rows to table>>=
for provider in get_all_providers():
    info = provider_info.get(provider.name, {})
    is_available = provider.is_available()
    configured_status = (
        "[green]Yes[/green]" if is_available else "[dim]No[/dim]"
    )
    if not getattr(provider, "default_enabled", True):
        configured_status += "[dim]*[/dim]"
    required = info.get("required", False)
    if not required:
        key_status = "[green]Optional[/green]"
    elif is_available:
        key_status = "Required"
    else:
        key_status = "[red]Required[/red]"
    table.add_row(
        provider.name,
        configured_status,
        key_status,
        info.get("env_var", "-"),
        info.get("how_to_get", ""),
    )
