\paragraph{An agent's reason.}
A decision that carries the agent's reason
([[sessions decide --reason]], \cref{sec:sessions-decide}) shows it on
a third line, with who gave it when the agent said: a reader scanning
the agent's discards should see why each was discarded without opening
the file.  The listing cuts a long reason at [[SHOW_REASON_CHARS]]
characters, marked with an ellipsis, so one wordy reason does not push
the list off the screen; the JSON form carries the three fields whole
([[agent_reason]], [[agent_by]], [[agent_decided_at]], [[null]] when
no reason was recorded), so a script never reads a cut reason.

<<sessions command>>=
SHOW_REASON_CHARS = 160


def agent_reason_line(decision) -> str:
    """The `sessions show` line with the agent's reason, or "" if none."""
    reason = decision.agent_reason
    if not reason:
        return ""
    if len(reason) > SHOW_REASON_CHARS:
        reason = reason[:SHOW_REASON_CHARS - 1].rstrip() + "…"
    by = f" ({decision.agent_by})" if decision.agent_by else ""
    return f"\n    [dim]reason{escape(by)}: {escape(reason)}[/dim]"
