\paragraph{Quotes in the machine reasons.}
A reason that quotes words its record does not hold
(\cref{sec:reason-quotes} in the review module) reads as evidence it
is not, and a reviewer looking at a screened session should see how
many there are and where.  When the session holds any machine reason,
an agent's or a classifier's, one line after \enquote{Decided by} says
how many reasons it holds, how many quote three or more words of their
record, and how many hold a quote not found in the record's title or
abstract; each paper with such a reason gets a mark after its title.
The JSON form gives every decision with such a reason its
[[unmatched_quotes]] (the key is absent otherwise, as for the other
optional fields) and, when the session holds a machine reason, the
counts per kind at the top level ([[reason_quotes]], with the number
of quotes left unchecked for being short), so the JSON of a session
without one is as it was.  The check runs once per decision, through
[[reason_quote_checks]], whose results the summary line, the marks and
the JSON all read, so a session of 30\,000 reasons is checked once per
command.  It compares with the record as the session holds it now: a
quote from a full-text passage, or from an abstract replaced since,
is listed as not found.

