The closing table of confirmed and changed machine decisions has the
rows of the report's summary ([[machine_review_rows]],
\cref{sec:report-provenance}), one group for the LLM and one for the
agent, so what the terminal says and what the document says agree.

[[sessions show]] ends with the copies of one work that the session
could not reconcile (\cref{sec:session-copies} in the review module).
Conflicting copies---a copy with a DOI and one without, decided
differently, or a DOI-less id under which a search also returned a work
of a distant year---and copies decided alike but not merged get a line
each, naming both ids, decisions and tags, or both years, so the user
can settle them with [[sessions decide --paper-id]].  The foldable
copies are counted with the command that folds them
(\cref{sec:sessions-reconcile}); the possible copies, which can run to
thousands, are only counted.  The JSON form lists the ids of both.  A
session without any prints nothing here.

