The second chance is checked end to end on a session of invented
records (issue~\#272): a chapter heading without authors, a book with
its edition in the title, and a heading and a book that reduce to the
same title.  The bibliography cites the first two the way a text
does, by the plain title with the [[edition]] field, cites the book
again as another edition, and cites the shared title.  The rows of the
first two must be cited, the count line must name the kind, and each
loosened and each ambiguous entry must be listed.  A bibliography whose
entries all match by DOI or work key, one of them with an [[edition]]
field, must print the count line as before and nothing more.

