\paragraph{Writing the export all or nothing.}
\label{sec:sessions-export-atomic}
An export of several files is only useful as a set: the [[.tex]] cites
keys from the [[.bib]], and a [[.csv]] next to them is expected to list the
same decisions.  [[sessions export -f all]] used to write the [[.csv]]
first and the [[.bib]] and [[.tex]] afterwards, so when the \LaTeX{} step
crashed (once on a list-valued venue) the user was left with a fresh
[[.csv]] beside a stale [[.tex]] that still compiled, and a traceback that
had scrolled past (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/83}).
A partial export is worse than none.

So the generators now write into a staging directory next to the targets
([[staged_outputs]], \cref{sec:atomic-write}), and the files are moved
into place only when every format has been built.  The generators need no
change: each receives a path in the staging directory under the final
file name, and the \LaTeX{} report derives its [[.bib]] from that path as
before.  Any failure, a bug in a generator as much as a missing output
directory, ends in one error line and exit code~1, with the previous
outputs untouched.  The traceback goes to the debug log, where
[[--verbose]] shows it.

<<write the export files all or nothing>>=
from scholar.utils import staged_outputs

out_base = Path(output)
files_created = []
tex_path = Path(f"{output}.tex")
try:
    with staged_outputs(out_base.parent) as staging:
        staged = staging / out_base.name

        if format_type in ("csv", "all"):
            generate_csv_report(session, Path(f"{staged}.csv"))
            files_created.append(Path(f"{output}.csv"))

        if format_type in ("latex", "all"):
            generate_latex_report(
                session, Path(f"{staged}.tex"), standalone=standalone
            )
            files_created.append(tex_path)
            files_created.append(tex_path.with_suffix(".bib"))

        if format_type == "table":
            default_label = "".join(
                c if c.isalnum() or c in "-_" else "_"
                for c in (session.name or session.query)[:30]
            )
            generate_audit_table(
                session,
                Path(f"{staged}.tex"),
                label=label or default_label,
                lang=lang,
                track=track,
                theme_names=theme_names,
                bearing_only=bearing_only,
                truncate_titles=truncate_titles,
                cited_works=cited_works,
            )
            files_created.append(tex_path)
except Exception as error:
    logger.debug("Export of %s failed", name, exc_info=True)
    console.print(
        f"[red]Export failed, no files were written or changed: "
        f"{escape(type(error).__name__)}: {escape(str(error))}[/red]"
    )
    raise typer.Exit(1)
@

