\subsection{Deciding non-interactively}
\label{sec:sessions-decide}

With [[search -n]] persisting sessions headlessly
(\cref{sec:search-session-persist}), the one remaining step that forced the
TUI open was recording the keep/discard decisions themselves.  [[sessions
decide]] closes that gap so the full review loop---search, screen, decide,
export---can run scripted or agent-driven
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/66}).

Papers are selected by DOI or by the session's paper id (the same id
[[sessions show --format json]] and the provenance tooling expose; it falls
back to a title-author hash when a paper has no DOI, so every paper is
addressable).  Both selectors are repeatable and can be mixed, and DOIs
compare case-insensitively since registries treat them so.

Two invariants mirror the TUI rather than trusting the caller:
\begin{description}
\item[Discarding requires a motivation] [[ReviewDecision.is_valid]] demands
  at least one tag on a discarded paper, so we refuse [[--discard]] without
  [[--tag]] up front instead of saving a session the TUI would consider
  invalid.
\item[All or nothing] If \emph{any} selector matches no paper in the
  session, nothing is saved and the exit code is nonzero.  A typo in one DOI
  of a batch must not leave the session half-updated---scripts can fix the
  selector and simply rerun.
\end{description}
Tags accumulate via [[add_tag]] (idempotent), so redeciding a paper refines
rather than clobbers its tags; the status change itself is an overwrite,
which is what redeciding means.

Decisions carry their provenance (\cref{sec:review-source}). An AI
agent that screens papers must not record its verdicts as human
decisions, because the audit table cites a human keep and the report
counts it as screened by the author; nor as an LLM's, because no
classifier run produced them. [[--source agent]] therefore stores the
decision as [[AGENT_UNREVIEWED]], and [[--source llm]], for an agent
that relays a classifier's verdicts, as [[LLM_UNREVIEWED]]. Both are
queued in the TUI for confirmation. Conversely, a human decision on
such a row \emph{is} the review: it goes through [[mark_as_reviewed]],
which mirrors the TUI (confirmed when the status stands, changed and
flagged as a training example when it does not) and keeps the machine's
name in the reviewed source, instead of overwriting the provenance with
[[HUMAN]] as it used to.

Who decided is no longer assumed when nobody is there to ask
(issue~\#162). The option used to default to [[human]], and an agent
that left it out (as the skill that drives it told it to) was recorded
as the author. Typing the command at a terminal is still a human
deciding, so the default stays [[human]] when standard input is a
terminal. Otherwise the command is run by a script or an agent, and it
refuses to guess: without [[--source]] it stops with exit status~2, the
status Typer uses for a usage error, before the session is loaded.

The new values have a cost outside this code.  A Scholar installed
before them reads [[agent]] and [[agent_reviewed]], like any value it
does not know, as [[human]], and writes [[human]] back when it next
saves the session, turning the agent's decisions into the author's
without a trace.  Old binaries cannot be fixed from here, so every
installation that touches a session must be updated before anyone
records a decision with [[--source agent]].

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("decide")
def sessions_decide(
    name: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Session name or query to record decisions in.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    keep: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option("--keep", help="Mark the selected papers as kept."),
    ] = False,
    discard: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--discard",
            help="Mark the selected papers as discarded (requires --tag).",
        ),
    ] = False,
    doi: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--doi",
            help="Select a paper by DOI (case-insensitive). Repeatable.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    paper_id: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--paper-id",
            help="Select a paper by its session paper id. Repeatable.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_paper_id,
        ),
    ] = None,
    tag: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--tag", "-t",
            help="Tag to attach: theme (kept) or motivation (discarded). "
                 "Repeatable.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    untag: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--untag",
            help="Tag to remove from every selected paper before --tag "
                 "adds its tags, e.g. an exclusion criterion left from "
