    keep_trace: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--keep-trace",
            help="With --source agent: keep the stored record of the "
                 "earlier classifier call (model, prompt version, "
                 "reason, date, truncation) instead of clearing it. "
                 "Needs -c. Refused with --source llm; no effect for a "
                 "human decision.",
        ),
    ] = False,
    reason: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--reason",
            help="With --source agent: the agent's reason for this "
                 "decision, stored on every selected paper with --by "
                 "and the time (at most 2000 characters).",
        ),
    ] = None,
    by: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--by",
            help="Who decided: with --source agent, who gave the "
                 "--reason or --reasons-file reasons (the agent's name "
                 "or role); with --source human, the human's name, "
                 "kept in the record of the review. Not guessed when "
                 "left out.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    reasons_file: Annotated[
        Optional[Path],
        typer.Option(
            "--reasons-file",
            help="With --source agent: select the papers and give each "
                 "its own reason, one per line as ID<TAB>REASON or "
                 "ID<TAB>REASON<TAB>CONFIDENCE. ID is doi:..., a bare "
                 "DOI or a session paper id (no https://doi.org/ "
                 "links). Columns are not quoted (not CSV): quote marks "
                 "are stored as written, and a reason cannot hold a "
                 "tab. Blank and # lines are skipped. Replaces "
                 "--doi/--paper-id.",
            exists=True, dir_okay=False, readable=True,
        ),
    ] = None,
    strict_quotes: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--strict-quotes",
            help="With --reason or --reasons-file: refuse the batch "
                 "(exit 2, nothing saved) when a reason quotes, between "
                 "double quote marks, three or more words that its "
                 "record's title and abstract do not hold. Without it "
                 "such quotes are listed on stderr and the batch is "
                 "saved.",
        ),
    ] = False,
) -> None:
    """
    Record keep/discard decisions in a saved session, without the TUI.

    Select papers by --doi and/or --paper-id (both repeatable). Discarding
    requires at least one --tag as motivation. If any selector matches
    nothing, no changes are saved and the exit code is nonzero.

    --source agent records an unreviewed decision of an AI agent, and
    --source llm one of a classifier, with the machine's --confidence if
    given (without it, any earlier confidence is cleared). A human
    decision on such a paper marks it reviewed, and changed if the
    status differs. Without --source the decision is a human one at a
    terminal; scripts and agents must pass --source. An agent or LLM
    decision never replaces one a human made or reviewed unless --force
    is given; otherwise the whole batch is refused (exit 2).

    --untag removes a tag (repeatable) before --tag adds its tags. When
    the status changes, or a --tag is a category (supports-claim, ...),
    the paper's old category tags are removed too, so a record holds one
    category (at most one category --tag is accepted); all other tags
    are kept. Otherwise the tags are added. An --untag is part of a
    decision like any other: an agent or LLM that untags without -c
    clears the confidence (pass -c again), and a human untag of an
    unreviewed agent or LLM decision counts as reviewing it.

    An id or DOI selects every decision under it. A session can hold a
    work twice under one id, decided apart (`sessions show` lists such
    copies); deciding them is refused (exit 2) unless --all-copies is
    given, which gives every copy this decision.

    An agent or LLM decision clears the fields an earlier classifier
    call stored (model, prompt version, reason, date), since they
    describe the decision being replaced. --keep-trace keeps them for
    an agent's correction made on top of that call (--source agent
    only; refused with --source llm, a new run whose trace would be
    taken for the old one's). It needs -c, so the confidence shown is
    the corrector's own. `sessions show` marks the kept fields as an
    earlier classifier call.

    --reason records why an agent decided (--source agent only; a
    classifier's reason is recorded by `scholar llm classify`), with
    --by naming the agent and the current time; every selected paper
    gets the same reason. --reasons-file gives each paper its own: its
    lines `ID<TAB>REASON` (ID a session paper id, or a DOI with or
    without `doi:`) are the selection, so it cannot be combined with
    --doi or --paper-id; an optional third column `<TAB>CONFIDENCE`
    (0-1) overrides -c for that line. Tabs are not allowed in a
    reason, and nothing is quoted: quote marks are stored as written.
    Status, tags and -c apply to the whole file, so group the
    lines by verdict. Any bad line, any id not in the session, or one
    id given two reasons aborts the batch unsaved. Reasons are
    stripped and must hold 1 to 2000 characters. An agent decision
    without a reason is recorded, with a warning. A later agent or
    LLM decision clears the reason (also with --keep-trace, which
    keeps only the classifier's record). A reason that is a placeholder
    (PLACEHOLDER, TODO, TBD, XXX, REASON, N/A) or has no letter or
    digit is refused, and so is a
    file line whose reason is only a number or a paper id (a shifted
    column).

    Each reason is checked against its own record: a quote of three or
    more words between double quote marks that the record's title and
    abstract do not hold is listed on stderr (line, id, quote), since
    it is a paraphrase or belongs to another record. The batch is saved
    all the same, unless --strict-quotes refuses it (exit 2).

    A human decision (--source human, also the default at a terminal)
    keeps a record of the review: the time, the channel (`decide`) and
    the name given with --by (not guessed). `sessions show` and the
    report count the human decisions with and without such a record;
    decisions made before it was kept have none, which does not mean
    a human did not make them. An agent or LLM decision clears it.

    Examples:
        scholar sessions decide my-review --source human --keep \\
            --doi 10.1145/3568813 --tag misconceptions
        scholar sessions decide my-review --source agent --discard \\
            --doi 10.1145/3568813 --tag off-topic-false-hit -c 0.9
        scholar sessions decide my-review --source agent --discard \\
            --doi 10.1145/3568813 --tag off-topic-false-hit -c 0.8 \\
            --keep-trace
        scholar sessions decide my-review --source agent --keep \\
            --doi 10.1145/3568813 --tag misconceptions -c 0.9 \\
            --reason "The abstract reports a misconception inventory." \\
            --by screening-agent
        scholar sessions decide my-review --source agent --discard \\
            --tag off-topic-false-hit -c 0.8 --by screening-agent \\
            --reasons-file discards.tsv
    """
    from scholar.review import (
        AGENT_AUDIT_FIELDS, AUDIT_CATEGORIES, CopyConflict, DecisionStatus,
        ReviewSource, clear_human_record, clear_machine_audit,
        copy_conflict_line, record_human_decision, same_id_pairs,
        save_session, tags_after_decision,
    )
    from scholar.llm_review import mark_as_reviewed
    from scholar.utils import utc_now_iso

