[[--source llm]] relays a classifier's verdict, and a classifier's
category must fit its decision: a discard does not take
[[supports-claim]] or [[qualifies-claim]], and a keep does not take
[[off-topic-false-hit]] ([[STATUS_CATEGORIES]],
\cref{sec:category-fits-status} in the LLM review module).  The
classifier withholds such an answer, so a relayed one must not slip
in through [[decide]]: it is a usage error (status~2), refused with
the other options before the session is loaded, naming the
categories that fit.  A human's or an agent's decision is free to
pair them, since the audit table shows a discarded bearing category
on purpose, as excluded (issue~\#89): a reviewer may exclude a
relevant hit under a rule of the review.  The rule's table lives with
the classifier, so it is imported only when a relayed verdict names a
category.

