Recording one decision has three cases. A machine decision (agent or
LLM) is stored as unreviewed, with [[is_example]] cleared since nobody
has corrected it yet, and with the audit fields of any earlier
classifier run cleared ([[clear_machine_audit]],
\cref{sec:review-source}), since they describe the decision being
replaced, unless [[--keep-trace]] asks to keep them for a correction
made on top of that run (below). A human decision on an unreviewed machine
decision is a review and is delegated to [[mark_as_reviewed]];
agreement means the status stands. Any other human decision simply
overwrites status and source.

<<record one decision with its source>>=
previous_status = decision.status
if source in MACHINE_DECISION_SOURCES:
    decision.status = status
    decision.source = ReviewSource(source)
    decision.is_example = False
    if not keep_trace:
        clear_machine_audit(decision)
    decision.llm_confidence = confidence
    <<record the agent's reason>>
elif decision.source.is_unreviewed:
    mark_as_reviewed(
        decision,
        user_agrees=decision.status == status,
        new_status=status,
    )
else:
    decision.status = status
    decision.source = ReviewSource.HUMAN
