<<replace the tags of a changed decision>>
@

The option's values are the stored values of the unreviewed sources,
so [[ReviewSource(source)]] turns one into the other.

A human decision, whichever branch recorded it, keeps the record of
the human's review (\cref{sec:human-review-record} in the review
module): the run's time, the channel [[decide]] and the name given with
[[--by]], or none, since a login guessed here would put a name on a
record its owner never made.  This is one of the two places where a
human decides (the TUI is the other), and the default at a terminal is
such a decision too, since that is what the default asserts.  A machine
decision clears the record instead: it replaces the human's decision
(with [[--force]], below) or a machine's, and either way no human
decision stands that the record could describe.  A later human decision
replaces the record, time included, since the record belongs to the
decision that stands.

<<keep the record of a human's review>>=
if source in MACHINE_DECISION_SOURCES:
    clear_human_record(decision)
else:
    record_human_decision(decision, "decide", by=by, at=decided_at)
@

Let's check the channel: a human decision records its time, channel
and name, one time for the run; a confirmation of an agent's call
records the same; a later decision by a human replaces the record; an
agent decision forced over a human one clears it; a reset paper decided
anew by a human gets a new one; and [[--by]] is accepted for a human
but still refused for a relayed classifier verdict.

