The reason, the name and the file's lines are checked by two small
functions, which return the problems instead of printing them, so that
every problem of a file is reported in one run.  The file is read as
bytes, so that Python's universal newlines do not turn a lone carriage
return inside a reason into a line end (below), and decoded as
[[utf-8-sig]], which drops a byte-order mark at its start: editors on
Windows and spreadsheets write one, and read as plain UTF-8 it would
stick to the first id, so the first line's paper would not be found
(or a first comment line would not start with [[#]]).

