Files come from editors and spreadsheets, not only from the agent's
own code.  A file saved with a byte-order mark still decides its first
line, whether that line is a paper or a comment.  Only a newline ends a
line: a reason copied from a PDF may hold a line separator (U+2028), a
next-line character or a form feed, which must stay in the stored
reason and must not shift the line numbers of the errors, which an
editor counts by newlines; a Windows line end is one line end.  Quote
marks are not syntax, so they are stored as written.

