Selection collects matches into a dict keyed by the decision object,
which both deduplicates (the same paper may be named by DOI \emph{and}
id) and gives a stable count for the summary.  A DOI or an id selects
every decision under it: a session can hold one work twice under one id
(\cref{sec:session-copies} in the review module), and a lookup of one
decision per id reached only the last of them
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/228}).  Unmatched
selectors are gathered rather than failing fast so one run reports
\emph{all} typos:

