Removing a tag is the other half of the tag rules
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/195}). The tests follow
the record through the sequence that exposed it, discarded under an
exclusion criterion and then kept, and check both rules at the command
line: [[--untag]] removes what it names, and a category among the
[[--tag]]s replaces the old one although the status stands.

