\paragraph{Placeholders, shifted columns and quotes.}
\label{sec:decide-quote-check}
A reasons file is written by a screener's script, and a check of
30\,000 such rows (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/256})
found what scripts get wrong: a reason left as the template's
\enquote{PLACEHOLDER}, lines whose columns had shifted so that the
reason column held a confidence or an id, a reason that quoted another
record because the rows of the screener's output and of the file had
slipped against each other, and paraphrases inside quote marks.  The
first two are malformed lines, refused like the others before the
session is loaded; the last two can only be seen against the record,
so they are checked once the ids are resolved, before anything is
saved.

A placeholder is a reason whose whole text, case-folded and stripped of
everything but letters and digits, is one of a short list.  Each entry
is there because a screener's template or script leaves it when the
real reason is missing: [[placeholder]] is what the issue found,
[[todo]] and [[tbd]] mark a reason to be written later, [[xxx]] is the
usual fill-in mark, [[reason]] is a template's own field name or a
column header taken for a row, and [[n/a]] (folded to [[na]]) says
that there is no reason.  The list is short on purpose: a real reason
of one word (\enquote{Duplicate}) must pass, and a word that only
\emph{might} be a placeholder is the screener's to judge.  A reason with
no letter or digit at all (\enquote{-}, \enquote{...}) says nothing
either and is refused as such.  The check
applies to [[--reason]] as well, through [[checked_agent_reason]],
since a placeholder typed on the command line is no more a reason.

<<sessions command>>=
REASON_PLACEHOLDERS = frozenset(
    {"placeholder", "todo", "tbd", "xxx", "reason", "na"}
)


def is_placeholder_reason(text: str) -> bool:
    """Whether `text` is a placeholder, not a reason (`REASON_PLACEHOLDERS`)."""
    folded = "".join(c for c in text.casefold() if c.isalnum())
    return folded in REASON_PLACEHOLDERS
@

A shifted column shows as a reason that is only a number (the
confidence, one column too early) or that is itself a paper id: it
starts with [[doi:]], [[hash:]] or [[10.]] and holds no space, as an
id does.  A reason that starts so and goes on in words is a sentence
(\enquote{doi:10.1/b is a duplicate of this record}), so the space is
the test.  This applies to
file lines only: a [[--reason]] has no columns to shift.

<<sessions command>>=
REASON_NUMBER = re.compile(r"[+-]?(?:\d+(?:[.,]\d*)?|[.,]\d+)")


def reason_column_shift(reason: str) -> str | None:
    """Describe a reasons-file reason that is a number or an id, if it is."""
    if REASON_NUMBER.fullmatch(reason):
        return (f"reason {reason!r} is only a number (a confidence in the "
                "reason column? columns shifted)")
    if (reason.casefold().startswith(("doi:", "hash:", "10."))
            and not any(c.isspace() for c in reason)):
        return f"reason {reason!r} is a paper id (columns shifted)"
    return None
@

Once the session is loaded and every id resolved, each line's reason is
checked against its own record with the review module's
[[unmatched_quotes]] (\cref{sec:reason-quotes} there): a quote of three
or more words that the record's title and abstract do not hold.  This is
where a row mix-up is cheapest to catch, before thirty thousand
decisions have been saved under the wrong reasons.  A [[--reason]],
one reason for many records, gets the same check for every record it
is given to.  The quotes not found are listed on standard error as
\enquote{line~N, id: "quote"} (or the paper id alone for [[--reason]]),
the first [[QUOTE_PROBLEMS_SHOWN]] of them, each cut at
[[QUOTE_SHOWN_CHARS]] characters, and the rest counted.  The batch is
then saved: a paraphrase is a weakness of the reason, not of the
decision, and scripts written before the check must keep working.
[[--strict-quotes]] refuses the batch instead, unsaved and with
status~2 like the other refusals, for a screener who wants a mix-up to
stop the run.  A record's id appears once per line, however many copies
the session holds under it.  The line that says the batch is saved all
the same is printed only when the command is about to save
([[saving]], which each command sets before the check): [[sessions
decide]] always is, [[sessions screen]] (\cref{sec:sessions-screen})
not on a dry run.

<<sessions command>>=
QUOTE_PROBLEMS_SHOWN = 20
QUOTE_SHOWN_CHARS = 80


def shown_quote(quote: str) -> str:
    """`quote` on one line, cut at `QUOTE_SHOWN_CHARS`, in quote marks."""
    quote = " ".join(quote.split())
    if len(quote) > QUOTE_SHOWN_CHARS:
        quote = quote[:QUOTE_SHOWN_CHARS - 1].rstrip() + "…"
    return f'"{quote}"'


def reason_quote_misses(decisions, trace_of: dict, reason) -> list[str]:
    """The quotes of the agent's reasons not found in their records.

    One `line N, ID: "quote"` (reasons file) or `ID: "quote"` (one
    `--reason`) per quote, in the order of the decisions.
    """
    from scholar.review import unmatched_quotes

    misses: list[str] = []
    seen: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()
    for decision in decisions:
        entry = trace_of.get(id(decision))
        given = entry.reason if entry is not None else reason
        if given is None:
            continue
        where = (f"line {entry.line}, {entry.paper}" if entry is not None
                 else decision.paper.id)
        if (where, decision.paper.id) in seen:
            continue
        seen.add((where, decision.paper.id))
        misses.extend(
            f"{where}: {shown_quote(quote)}"
            for quote in unmatched_quotes(given, decision.paper)
        )
    return misses
<<check the quotes of the agent's reasons>>=
quote_misses = reason_quote_misses(selected.values(), trace_of, reason)
if quote_misses:
    errors = Console(stderr=True)
    errors.print(
        "[yellow]Quotes not found in the record's title or abstract "
        f"({len(quote_misses)}):[/yellow]"
    )
    for miss in quote_misses[:QUOTE_PROBLEMS_SHOWN]:
        errors.print(f"  {escape(miss)}", soft_wrap=True, highlight=False)
    if len(quote_misses) > QUOTE_PROBLEMS_SHOWN:
        errors.print(
            f"  ... and {len(quote_misses) - QUOTE_PROBLEMS_SHOWN} more"
        )
    if strict_quotes:
        console.print(
            "[red]--strict-quotes: a reason quotes words its record "
            "does not hold.[/red]"
        )
        console.print("[yellow]No changes saved.[/yellow]")
        raise typer.Exit(2)
    if saving:
        errors.print(
            "[yellow]Saved all the same; --strict-quotes refuses such a "
            "batch.[/yellow]"
        )
