\subsection{Correcting who decided}
\label{sec:sessions-relabel}

A decision can carry the wrong source: an agent that ran [[sessions
decide]] before [[--source]] was required off a terminal was recorded
as the author ([[human]]), and its confirmations of an LLM's calls as
[[llm_reviewed]] (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/216}).
[[sessions decide]] cannot repair that: a machine source on a human's
decision is refused, and with [[--force]] the paper is decided anew,
which clears the classifier's record and confidence.  [[sessions
relabel]] changes the source and leaves the decision as it is, through
[[relabel_source]] (\cref{sec:relabel-source} of the review module,
which explains why only [[agent]] and [[llm]] can be given, why an
LLM call an agent confirmed becomes [[agent]], not
[[agent_reviewed]], and why the training-example flag moves into the
relabel record).

[[--from]] is required and names the sources to correct, so that a
batch never touches a decision whose source the caller did not mean:
with [[--all]], only the decided papers with one of those sources are
relabelled.  It is repeatable, and a value may also list several
sources separated by commas, as in [[--from human,llm_reviewed]].
Papers are selected as in [[sessions decide]] (\cref{sec:sessions-decide}),
by [[--doi]] and [[--paper-id]], or all of them with [[--all]]; one of
the two forms is required, so that no bare command relabels a whole
session.  A selector that matches no paper aborts the batch unsaved, as
in [[sessions decide]].  A selected paper that is pending or has another
source is left alone and named, not an error: a script that relabels a
list twice should not fail the second time.  Unlike [[decide]], a
selector picks every decision of that paper, since a session can hold
one paper twice (\cref{sec:session-copies}) and a correction of who
decided applies to each record of it.

The checks that need no session run first, with exit status~2 like any
usage error: a target that claims a human's confirmation is refused
with the reason and where a human confirms instead, and so is a target
that is also among the [[--from]] sources, which would change nothing.
A [[--from]] value Scholar does not know is accepted only if some
decision in the session holds it (as [[manual]] does in real sessions,
\cref{sec:review-source}); otherwise it is a misspelling and is refused
too.  The target is never [[human]], so there is nothing to ask a
terminal about: the command runs the same for a person and for a
script.

The command prints how many decisions went from which source to which.
With [[--dry-run]] it prints the same counts and writes nothing, not
even the backup.  Otherwise it first copies the session file with
[[keep_copy_before_run]] under the label [[pre-relabel]], as [[scholar
enrich]] does (\cref{sec:enrich-chunks}): a relabel of a whole session
is one save, so [[.bak]] would cover it as well, but a second run (say
with another [[--from]]) would overwrite that, while the labelled copies
are kept for the last three runs.  All records of one run carry one
time, taken from the review module's clock seam [[_utcnow]], the same
one that names the copy, the caller's [[--note]] (why) and [[--by]]
(who made or asked for the correction).  Who is only recorded when the
caller says it: a login name would name the account that ran the
command, which for an agent's run is the author's, the very confusion
this command corrects.  The session is saved with [[save_session]],
which takes the lock and merges what other processes saved meanwhile.

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("relabel")
def sessions_relabel(
    name: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Session name or query whose decisions to relabel.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    from_sources: Annotated[
        list[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--from",
            help="Source to correct: only decided papers with this "
                 "source are relabelled (human, llm_reviewed, "
                 "agent_reviewed, agent, llm or a stored unknown value). "
                 "Repeatable or comma-separated.",
        ),
    ],
    to: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Option(
            "--to",
            help="The source they get: agent or llm. A human's "
                 "confirmation (human, llm_reviewed, agent_reviewed) is "
                 "refused: a human gives it in the TUI or with "
                 "`sessions decide --source human`.",
            autocompletion=complete_relabel_target,
        ),
    ],
    doi: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--doi",
            help="Select a paper by DOI (case-insensitive). Repeatable.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    paper_id: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--paper-id",
            help="Select a paper by its session paper id. Repeatable.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_paper_id,
        ),
    ] = None,
    all_papers: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--all",
            help="Select every paper (still only those with a --from "
                 "source).",
        ),
    ] = False,
    dry_run: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--dry-run",
            help="Print what would be relabelled; write nothing.",
        ),
    ] = False,
    note: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--note",
            help="Why the source is corrected, kept with each record.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    by: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--by",
            help="Who made or asked for the correction, kept with each "
                 "record as given (nothing is recorded without it).",
        ),
    ] = None,
) -> None:
    """
    Correct who decided, keeping the decisions themselves.

    Sets the source of the selected decided papers whose source is a
    --from source to --to (agent or llm), and changes nothing else:
    status, tags, confidence and the LLM classifier's record stay. The
    training-example flag is cleared (an unreviewed decision is no
    example) and kept in the record. Each relabelled decision records
    the change (from, to, time, --note, --by), shown by `sessions show`
    and the CSV export. Pending papers are never relabelled.

    Select papers with --doi and/or --paper-id, or --all. If a selector
    matches nothing, nothing is saved (exit 1). The session file is
    copied to `<name>.json.pre-relabel-<time>.bak` before it is saved;
    --dry-run writes nothing.

    Examples:
        scholar sessions relabel my-review --from human --to agent --all \\
            --note "recorded by an agent before --source was required" \\
            --by "the author"
        scholar sessions relabel my-review --from llm_reviewed --to agent \\
            --doi 10.1145/3568813 --dry-run
    """
    from collections import Counter

    from scholar.review import (
        ReviewSource, SessionFileError, _utcnow, keep_copy_before_run,
        relabel_source, save_session,
    )

    console = Console()
    <<validate relabel options>>
    try:
        session = open_session_argument(name, strict=True)
    except SessionFileError as error:
        exit_on_unreadable_session(error)
    if session is None:
        console.print(f"[red]Session not found: {escape(name)}[/red]")
        raise typer.Exit(1)
    <<refuse an unknown [[--from]] source nobody holds>>
    <<select the decisions to relabel>>

    changes = Counter((d.source.value, target.value) for d in chosen)
    verb = "Would relabel" if dry_run else "Relabelled"
    console.print(
        f"{verb} {len(chosen)} decision(s) in session '{escape(name)}':"
    )
    for (old, new), count in changes.items():
        console.print(f"  {escape(old)} -> {escape(new)}: {count}")
    if dry_run or not chosen:
        return
    copy = keep_copy_before_run(session, "pre-relabel")
    at = _utcnow().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
    for decision in chosen:
        relabel_source(decision, target, at, note, by)
    save_session(session)
    if copy is not None:
        console.print(f"[dim]Copy of the session before: {copy}[/dim]")
