The target list is the review module's, so that the command and
[[relabel_source]] cannot disagree on what may be given; it is looked
up when the command runs, as every command that needs the review
module imports it: importing [[scholar.cli]] does not load it.  The
two helpers go with the other completion functions, which are defined
before the commands that name them.

<<completion functions>>=
def relabel_targets():
    """The sources `sessions relabel --to` accepts (`RELABEL_TARGETS`)."""
    from scholar.review import RELABEL_TARGETS

    return RELABEL_TARGETS


def complete_relabel_target(incomplete: str) -> list[str]:
    """Complete the --to of `sessions relabel`."""
    return [
        s.value for s in relabel_targets()
        if s.value.startswith(incomplete)
    ]
