\subsection{Giving an abstract found by hand}
\label{sec:sessions-set-abstract}

When [[scholar enrich]] finds no abstract, a screener who looks the DOI
up by hand can store what they found with [[sessions set-abstract]]
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/258}).  The command
is a thin layer over [[set_abstract]] (\cref{sec:set-abstract} of the
review module, which explains why the origin is recorded on the
decision, how the text is cleaned and how the record survives merges,
folds and appends).

A paper is selected with [[--paper-id]] or [[--doi]], as in [[sessions
decide]], and the text read from [[--file]], or from standard input
with [[--file -]], so that a text with quotes, dollar signs or line
breaks need not survive a shell's quoting.  [[--from]] is required: an
abstract with no origin is what the command exists to prevent, since
nothing would then tell it from a provider's.  The batch form
[[--abstracts-file]] takes lines [[ID<TAB>FROM<TAB>ABSTRACT]] instead,
by the conventions of [[sessions decide --reasons-file]]
(\cref{sec:sessions-decide}): read as [[utf-8-sig]], lines ended by
newlines only, blank and [[#]] lines skipped, the id a session paper id
or a DOI (bare or with [[doi:]]), the columns not quoted.  A line has
three columns, the last running to its end (below), and every bad line
is named in one run, with
exit status~2 before the session is loaded.  [[--by]] names who found
the text, and is recorded only when given.

After loading, a selector that matches no paper aborts the run unsaved
with exit status~1, all of them named, as in [[sessions decide]].  A
selector takes the paper, with every decision of the session that
holds it.  Two lines that give one paper different texts or origins
are refused (exit status~2); the same line twice is harmless.  A paper
that already has an abstract is refused, all of them named and nothing
saved (exit status~2), unless [[--replace]] is given; the replaced text
is then kept in the record.

A record found missing an abstract may be one of two copies of a work
in the session, its twin holding the abstract, or the abstract would
land on the copy that is later folded away.  A screener reported that
many records whose abstracts they had found by hand were copies of
records already in the session.  So when the paper has a possible copy
([[possible_copies]]) or a foldable copy ([[foldable_copies]], both
\cref{sec:session-copies} of the review module), a note on standard
error names the copy and points to [[sessions reconcile]] and
[[sessions show]].  The abstract is still set: a possible copy is not
certainly a copy, and a fold carries the record, with the text, to the
survivor.  When the paper has no DOI and the copy is a DOI record that
already holds an abstract, the note says so: a fold keeps the DOI
copy's abstract, so the hand text would then survive only in the
record.

The command prints what it sets, per paper, with the number of
characters.  [[--dry-run]] prints the same and writes nothing.
Otherwise the session file is first copied with
[[keep_copy_before_run]] under the label [[pre-set-abstract]], as
[[sessions reset]] does, and saved with [[save_session]], which takes
the lock and merges what other processes saved meanwhile.  All records
of one run carry one time from the review module's clock seam
[[_utcnow]].

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("set-abstract")
def sessions_set_abstract(
    name: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Session name or query holding the paper.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    paper_id: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--paper-id",
            help="Select the paper by its session paper id.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_paper_id,
        ),
    ] = None,
    doi: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--doi",
            help="Select the paper by DOI (case-insensitive).",
        ),
    ] = None,
    text_file: Annotated[
        Optional[Path],
        typer.Option(
            "--file",
            help="Read the abstract from this file; - reads standard "
                 "input.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    origin: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--from",
            help="Where the abstract was found, e.g. \"Crossref, "
                 "2026-11-20\" (required with --file).",
        ),
    ] = None,
    by: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--by",
            help="Who found the abstract, kept with the record as given "
                 "(nothing is recorded without it).",
        ),
    ] = None,
    abstracts_file: Annotated[
        Optional[Path],
        typer.Option(
            "--abstracts-file",
            help="Set several abstracts, one per line as "
                 "ID<TAB>FROM<TAB>ABSTRACT. ID is doi:..., a bare DOI or "
                 "a session paper id. Columns are not quoted (not CSV); "
                 "tabs inside the abstract become spaces. Blank and # "
                 "lines are skipped. Replaces --paper-id, --doi, --file "
                 "and --from.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    replace: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--replace",
            help="Replace an abstract the paper already has (the old one "
                 "is kept in the record).",
        ),
    ] = False,
    dry_run: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--dry-run",
            help="Print what would be set; write nothing.",
        ),
    ] = False,
) -> None:
    """
    Store an abstract found by hand, with where it was found.

    For a record `scholar enrich` found no abstract for. The text is
    cleaned (entities, inline markup, broken encodings, white space)
    and becomes the paper's abstract; the decision records where it was
    found (--from), who found it (--by), when, and its length, shown
    by `sessions show`, the CSV export and the report. A paper that
    already has an abstract is refused (exit 2) unless --replace. If a
    paper is not in the session, nothing is saved (exit 1). The session
    file is copied to `<name>.json.pre-set-abstract-<time>.bak` before
    it is saved; --dry-run writes nothing.

    Examples:
        scholar sessions set-abstract my-review --doi 10.1234/example \\
            --file abstract.txt --from "Crossref, 2026-11-20"
        pbpaste | scholar sessions set-abstract my-review \\
            --paper-id hash:3f2a... --file - --from "PubMed, PMID 123"
        scholar sessions set-abstract my-review --abstracts-file found.tsv
    """
    import sys

    from scholar.review import (
        LONG_ABSTRACT_CHARS, SessionFileError, _utcnow,
        clean_abstract_text, keep_copy_before_run, save_session,
        set_abstract,
    )

    console = Console()
    errors = Console(stderr=True)
    <<validate set-abstract options>>
    <<read the abstracts to set>>
    try:
        session = open_session_argument(name, strict=True)
    except SessionFileError as error:
        exit_on_unreadable_session(error)
    if session is None:
        console.print(f"[red]Session not found: {escape(name)}[/red]")
        raise typer.Exit(1)
    <<find the papers to give abstracts>>
    <<refuse to replace an abstract without [[--replace]]>>
    <<note possible copies of the papers>>

    verb = "Would set" if dry_run else "Set"
    console.print(
        f"{verb} the abstract of {len(targets)} paper(s) in session "
        f"'{escape(name)}':"
    )
    for paper, (decisions, entry) in targets.items():
        old = next((d.paper.abstract for d in decisions
                    if d.paper.abstract), None)
        replacing = f", replacing {len(old)}" if old else ""
        console.print(
            f"  {escape(paper)}: {len(entry.text)} characters from "
            f"{escape(entry.origin)}{replacing}",
            soft_wrap=True,
        )
    if dry_run:
        return
    copy = keep_copy_before_run(session, "pre-set-abstract")
    at = _utcnow().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
    for decisions, entry in targets.values():
        set_abstract(decisions, entry.text, entry.origin, at, by, replace)
    save_session(session)
    if copy is not None:
        console.print(f"[dim]Copy of the session before: {copy}[/dim]")
