A screener may not screen a decision it made itself: when the
screener's kind and name are those of the snapshot a selected paper's
decision gives ([[verdict_screener]]), the batch is refused, unsaved,
with status~2 and those papers named.  Such a verdict is the same
screener again, and two things make it useless as a second screen.
Agreement of a screener with itself (test and retest) is not computed
in this version, so the record would only be read as a second
screener's.  And a comparison of screeners takes the latest record of
each screener, so a second record under the decision's own identity
would replace the first verdict and hide it, and with it any
disagreement.  A screener who now thinks otherwise changes the
decision, with [[sessions decide]].

<<refuse a screener screening its own decision>>=
own = {}
for decision in selected.values():
    screener = verdict_screener(decision)
    if decision.is_decided and (screener["kind"], screener["name"]) \
            == (as_kind, by):
        own[decision.paper.id] = decision
for paper in own:
    console.print(
        f"[red]{escape(paper)}: {escape(as_kind)} {escape(by)} made this "
        "decision[/red]",
        soft_wrap=True,
    )
if own:
    console.print(
        "[red]This screener made the decision; a change of mind is a "
        "`scholar sessions decide`, not a second screening.[/red]\n"
        "[yellow]No changes saved.[/yellow]",
        soft_wrap=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(2)
