[[scholar rq]] classifies its results with the same classifier
(\cref{sec:research-questions}), so it can leave papers pending for the same
reasons; it lists them with the same function, after its summary.

The classifier also withholds the decision of a paper whose answer is
unusable (\cref{sec:llm-parse} in the LLM review module): no answer,
a decision it cannot read, a missing or out-of-range confidence.
Those are listed under their own heading, because the remedy differs:
a category problem is about the vocabulary, an unusable answer about
the model, and the next batch may well answer it.

The summary reaches the user even though the other decisions of the
batch were applied and saved:

