\subsection{Quotes in the classifier's reasons}
\label{sec:llm-classify-quotes}

The model gives a reason for each decision, stored as [[llm_reason]],
and a reason that quotes the record is read as evidence.  A model can
put its own paraphrase between quote marks, or words from another
paper of the batch, just as an agent can
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/256}).  So the run
ends with one line when any decision it applied has a reason quoting
three or more words that the record does not hold
([[unmatched_quotes]], \cref{sec:reason-quotes} in the review module):
the number of such decisions and the first [[LLM_QUOTE_MISSES_SHOWN]]
of them, each as its paper id and its first quote not found.

The quotes are compared with the title, the abstract and the full-text
passages the model was shown ([[--full-text]]), which the batch hands
back ([[LLMBatchResult.passages]]) because they are not stored: this
run is the only place where a quote from a passage can be found.
[[sessions show]] later checks against the title and abstract only, so
such a quote is listed there as not found.  The reason checked is the
stored one, cut at [[MAX_REASON_CHARS]]; a quote whose closing mark was
cut off is no longer a quote.  Nothing is withheld or retried for it:
the verdict may well be right, and the line tells the reviewer which
reasons to read before trusting their quotes.

<<report reasons quoting words not in the record>>=
print_reason_quote_misses(console, updated, result.passages)
<<llm command>>=
LLM_QUOTE_MISSES_SHOWN = 3


def print_reason_quote_misses(console, decisions, passages: dict) -> None:
    """One line on the classifier's reasons quoting words not in the record."""
    from scholar.review import unmatched_quotes

    misses = []
    for decision in decisions:
        unmatched = unmatched_quotes(
            decision.llm_reason, decision.paper,
            passages.get(decision.paper.id, ()),
        )
        if unmatched:
            misses.append(f"{decision.paper.id}: {shown_quote(unmatched[0])}")
    if not misses:
        return
    shown = "; ".join(misses[:LLM_QUOTE_MISSES_SHOWN])
    more = len(misses) - LLM_QUOTE_MISSES_SHOWN
    console.print(
        f"[yellow]Reasons quoting words not in the record "
        f"({len(misses)}):[/yellow] {escape(shown)}"
        + (f" (and {more} more; see sessions show)" if more > 0 else ""),
        soft_wrap=True, highlight=False,
    )
