\subsection{Sampling LLM decisions for review}
\label{sec:llm-sample-command}

[[scholar llm sample]] draws a seeded random sample of unreviewed LLM
decisions for a human to review, and later reports how often the human
changed them (\cref{sec:llm-sample} in the LLM review module).  One
command does both, because they are two halves of one procedure: the
draw records the sample in the sessions, and [[--report]] reads it
back.

Drawing needs the criteria spelled out: [[--discarded]], [[--kept]] or
both, a size [[-n]] and a [[--seed]].  The seed has no default on
purpose: a seed picked for the user would still be recorded, but a
seed the user chose and wrote in their protocol is one the methods
section can name before the sample is drawn.  Missing criteria are a
usage error (exit code 2) and nothing is drawn.  The sample is
recorded in every session given, which are then saved; the drawn
papers are printed with their ids, so that each can be reviewed with
[[sessions decide]] (the TUI's filter [[s]] lists them too).

[[--report]] reports every sample stored in the given sessions.  A
sample pooled over other sessions as well is reported over all of
them: the other sessions are read read-only, from the files the
sample recorded ([[pooled_sample_sessions]], which also says why not by
name), and one that no longer exists is counted as \enquote{not
found}.  [[-f json]] gives the same
numbers for scripts, with the unreviewed papers listed by session and
id.

<<llm command>>=
@llm_app.command("sample")
def llm_sample(
    session_names: Annotated[
        list[str],
        typer.Argument(
            help="Sessions to sample from (pooled), or to report on.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    discarded: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option("--discarded", help="Sample unreviewed LLM discards."),
    ] = False,
    kept: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option("--kept", help="Sample unreviewed LLM inclusions."),
    ] = False,
    min_confidence: Annotated[
        Optional[float],
        typer.Option(
            "--min-confidence",
            help="Only decisions with at least this LLM confidence (0-1).",
        ),
    ] = None,
    max_confidence: Annotated[
        Optional[float],
        typer.Option(
            "--max-confidence",
            help="Only decisions with an LLM confidence below this (0-1, "
            "exclusive), so --min-confidence 0.5 --max-confidence 0.7 and "
            "--min-confidence 0.7 do not overlap.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    no_confidence: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--no-confidence",
            help="Only decisions without an LLM confidence.",
