\subsection{CSV formatter}

For scripting and shell pipelines, we provide a tab-separated CSV format.
This is especially useful when output is piped to other commands.
We include metadata as a comment header so consumers know the search context.
The [[# Results:]] line is the count a script records per query and
provider, so it is where a failure must show: it reads
[[failed (reason)]] instead of 0 (or [[N, incomplete (reason)]]),
deliberately not a number, so a script that parses it stops instead of
recording a zero.  Retries get a line of their own, which keeps the
count of an answered search a plain number, and so do the total the
provider reported ([[# Total reported:]]) and a count that stopped at
the limit ([[# Capped at limit:]]), for the same reason
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/166}).  A merged result
adds one [[# Search:]] line per provider with that provider's own
outcome (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/164}):

<<formatter classes>>=
class CSVFormatter:
    """Output results as tab-separated values for scripting."""

    def format(self, results: list) -> None:
        """Output results as CSV with metadata header."""
        for result in results:
            # Metadata header as comments
            print(f"# Query: {result.query}")
            print(f"# Provider: {result.provider}")
            print(f"# Timestamp: {result.timestamp}")
            label = hits_label(
                len(result.papers), result.error,
                ranked=is_ranked_provider(result.provider),
            )
            print(f"# Results: {label}")
            if result.retries:
                print(f"# Retries: {result.retries}")
            total, estimated = result_total(result)
            if total is not None:
                about = " (estimate)" if estimated else ""
                print(f"# Total reported: {total}{about}")
            if (not result.error and result.limit
                    and not getattr(result, "parts", None)
                    and len(result.papers) == result.limit
                    and (total is None or total > len(result.papers))):
                print(f"# Capped at limit: {result.limit}")
            for line in part_hits_lines(result):
                print(f"# Search: {line}")
            print()

            # Header row
            print("title\tauthors\tyear\tdoi\tvenue\turl")

            # Data rows
            for paper in result.papers:
                authors = "; ".join(paper.authors)
                year = str(paper.year) if paper.year else ""
                print(f"{paper.title}\t{authors}\t{year}\t"
                      f"{paper.doi or ''}\t{paper.venue or ''}\t"
                      f"{paper.url or ''}")
            print()
@

