\subsection{JSON formatter}

For scripting, we provide JSON output that includes all paper metadata,
including the open-access fields ([[pdf_url]], [[oa_status]]) so a script can
pick out the papers it can fetch.
We also surface the [[filters]] and [[limit]] that were applied, so a consumer
reading the JSON has the same provenance the [[bibtex+prov]] export
reconstructs --- the search is fully described by its query, providers,
filters, and limit, and JSON is the natural place to expose all four to a
machine reader.  The [[error]] and [[retries]] of the result go along
for the same reason: a consumer counting papers must be able to tell a
failed provider from an empty answer.  So do the [[total]] the provider
reported (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/166}) and, for a
merged result, the [[searches]] it was made of, each with its own
count, total and error (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/164}).

<<formatter classes>>=
class JSONFormatter:
    """Output results as JSON for scripting."""

    def format(self, results: list) -> None:
        """Output results as JSON."""
        output = []
        for result in results:
            output.append({
                "query": result.query,
                "provider": result.provider,
                "timestamp": result.timestamp,
                "filters": result.filters,
                "limit": result.limit,
                "error": result.error,
                "retries": result.retries,
                "total": result_total(result)[0],
                "total_estimated": result_total(result)[1],
                **({"searches": [
                    {
                        "query": part.query,
                        "provider": part.provider,
                        "hits": len(part.papers),
                        "total": result_total(part)[0],
                        "total_estimated": result_total(part)[1],
                        "error": part.error,
                        "retries": part.retries,
                    }
                    for part in result.parts
                ]} if getattr(result, "parts", None) else {}),
                "papers": [
                    {
                        "title": p.title,
                        "authors": p.authors,
                        "affiliations": p.affiliations,
                        "year": p.year,
                        "doi": p.doi,
                        "abstract": p.abstract,
                        "venue": p.venue,
                        "url": p.url,
                        "pdf_url": p.pdf_url,
                        "oa_status": p.oa_status,
                    }
                    for p in result.papers
                ],
            })
        print(json.dumps(output, indent=2))
@

