The [[DATE]] of a cached answer is the date it was fetched, not the
day of the run, and a cached answer without a known fetch date says
so; in a merged result each paper is dated by the providers that
returned it (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/167}):

<<test functions>>=
    def test_bibtex_prov_date_is_the_fetch_date(self, capsys):
        """DATE gives when the answer was fetched, never the run's day."""
        cached = SearchResult(
            query="q", provider="openalex",
            timestamp="2026-11-18T10:00:00",
            papers=[Paper(title="Old", authors=["Alice"], year=2024)],
            searched_at="2026-11-18T09:00:00+00:00",
            fetched_at="2026-10-02T08:00:00+00:00", from_cache=True,
        )
        unknown = SearchResult(
            query="q", provider="dblp", timestamp="2026-11-18T10:00:00",
            papers=[Paper(title="Older", authors=["Bob"], year=2020)],
            searched_at="2026-11-18T09:00:00+00:00", from_cache=True,
        )
