The provenance block now names the paper it belongs to
(\cref{sec:prov-paper-id}).  Let's verify that the stub carries the id
and that an import keys the note by it even for a title whose escapes
cannot be undone and no note exists yet, the case the title match could
not reach; that an export writes the id of the note it found and an
import does not store it in the note; that a file without the line still
finds a note when the escaper changed the author's name too
([[Conan O’Brien]]); that a note imported from a hand-escaped [[.bib]]
before this change, keyed by the escaped text, is continued rather than
doubled; that an entry whose unescaped id has a note never lists every
note; and that an import keeps the title a note already has, which the
entry holds only escaped.

