\section{Entry Point}
\label{sec:cli-main}

The main entry point runs the Typer application.
It registers nothing itself: the snowball and tuxedo subcommands are part of
the application's group class and are imported only when they run
(\cref{sec:lazy-subcommands}).

Many commands read or write notes and per-query decisions, from the
[[notes]] commands to the TUI.  When that file is unreadable, or a write
fails, the notes module raises [[NotesFileError]] instead of carrying on
with an empty store and overwriting the file
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/114}).  Rather than catch it
in every command, we catch it once here and turn it into one line that
names the file and points to its [[.bak]], with exit code~1.

<<main entry point>>=
def main() -> None:
    """Main entry point for the Scholar CLI."""
    from scholar.notes import NotesFileError
    from scholar.utils import backup_path

    try:
        app()
    except NotesFileError as error:
        Console(stderr=True).print(
            f"[red]{escape(str(error))}[/red]\n"
            "Nothing was overwritten. Repair the file or restore its "
            f"previous version from {escape(str(backup_path(error.path)))}."
        )
        sys.exit(1)
@

A corrupt notes file therefore ends [[scholar notes list]] with that line
and exit code~1, and the file is left as it was:

<<test functions>>=
def test_main_reports_unreadable_notes_file(tmp_path, monkeypatch, capsys):
    """main() turns NotesFileError into one line and exit code 1."""
    from scholar.notes import NOTES_FILE, get_data_dir, invalidate_notes_cache

    monkeypatch.setenv("SCHOLAR_DATA_DIR", str(tmp_path))
    invalidate_notes_cache()
    notes_file = get_data_dir() / NOTES_FILE
    notes_file.write_text('{"doi:10.1/x": ')
    monkeypatch.setattr(sys, "argv", ["scholar", "notes", "list"])
    with pytest.raises(SystemExit) as exit_info:
        main()
    assert exit_info.value.code == 1
    err = capsys.readouterr().err
    assert "Cannot read notes file" in " ".join(err.split())
    assert "paper_notes.json.bak" in "".join(err.split())
    assert notes_file.read_text() == '{"doi:10.1/x": '
